<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh April copper output up 10 pct to 26,000 T.</title>
<headline>Kazakh April copper output up 10 pct to 26,000 T.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakh copper output rose to 26,003 tonnes in April from 23,633 tonnes in March, an increase of 10.0 percent, the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It gave the following figures for non-ferrous metals production (all figures in tonnes).</p>
<p>				Apr 97	 Mar 97	Jan-Apr 97</p>
<p>  Copper		   26,003	 23,633	  87,690</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change  +10.0	  +27.6	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change   +4.5	  -11.0	   -12.5</p>
<p> Zinc			14,792	 15,147	  58,138</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change   -2.3	   +6.9	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change  +13.4	  +10.1	   +11.7</p>
<p> Lead			 8,148	  8,244	  22,980</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change   -1.2	  +57.9	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change  +79.5	  +88.3	   +15.7</p>
<p> Bauxite		  242,500	252,100	 953,200</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change   -3.8	   -9.0	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change   -3.0	   -5.9	    -0.5</p>
<p> Alumina		   89,277	 94,883	 362,361</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change   -5.9	  +10.0	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change   +2.9	   +6.0	    +3.7</p>
<p> Titanium		   1,500	  1,540	   6,040</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change   -2.6	   +2.7	     n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change  +75.0	  +64.2	   +67.1</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
